From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Lamb <paul@paulscode.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:18:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] Backfill: index blocks below where a pruned node's
 index starts

Opt-in (index.backfillFromHeight, index.backfillSpeed): from the chosen block up
to the index's first block, oldest first, after the index has caught up with the
tip. Blocks come from the node, its btc-rpc-proxy, or getblockfrompeer, checked
against the node's header (hash, Merkle root, witness commitment); prevouts come
from the scriptPubKey cache or the Electrum backend, each transaction checked
against its txid. One transaction per block with the position, so a stop resumes
where it left off; connected wallets are scanned over each backfilled range.
